      id: "front-trap",
      term: "Front trap",
      aka: ["Trap in front", "Front machine"],
      cat: "Layout",
      short_en: "A trap placed in front of the line of stands, usually throwing crossing, quartering or rabbit targets across the field.",
      short_uk: "Машинка перед лінією номерів, що зазвичай кидає поперечні, навскісні мішені чи кролика через поле.",
      long_en: "Front traps stand in or at the edge of the field in front of the shooters, hidden behind screens or in a low pit. They typically throw targets across the field, angled away from or towards the line, or along the ground as rabbits. Because the shooter moves along five stands, a front target that is a straight crosser from stand 3 becomes a quartering target from stand 1 or 5. Front traps must be protected so that shot cannot hit the trapper or the machine.",
