      long_en: "A rear trap stands behind the shooters, protected so that it cannot be hit, and throws targets over or beside the line into the field. The shooter therefore sees the target only when it appears above or beside him and must react quickly to a going-away or quartering-away target. Because the shooter cannot see the trap, a clear call and a predictable release are especially important. The rear trap is a typical Compak feature that Trap shooters find unusual, since in Trap all targets come from in front.",
